# How-it-works docs (product understanding)

After meaningful implementation (and after user **go**), keep `Docs/how-it-works/` accurate. This is **not** a second Worklog.

## Split (do not merge these jobs)

| Location | Job |
|----------|-----|
| `Worklog/` (repo root) | Short memory: what changed, paths, how to retest. Ruled by `04-worklog.mdc`. |
| `Docs/how-it-works/` | How the **product** behaves: user flow, server flow, mock vs live, rules layers. |

**Never** put Worklog under `Docs/`. **Never** invent `Docs/Worklog/`.

## Folder layout

```text
Docs/
  how-it-works/
    00-overview.md
    features/
      <feature-slug>.md
```

Create on first meaningful feature if missing.

## When to update
- After a vertical slice / API / demo-path change that alters behaviour.
- Skip for typos, pure CSS tweaks, or one-line renames unless the user asks.

## Token caps
- No source-code dumps. Numbered workflows + file paths only.
- `00-overview.md` prefer **≤100 lines**.
- Each feature doc prefer **≤60 lines**.
- New chat: default `@Worklog/_ARCHITECTURE.md`. Add `@Docs/how-it-works/00-overview.md` only when the task needs product-flow understanding. Do **not** load every how-it-works file every turn.
- No API keys, tokens, connection strings, or `.env` values in Docs.

## `00-overview.md` required shape

```markdown
# How The App Works

## User Flow
1. What the user opens
2. What they enter or click
3. Request the browser sends (shape only, no secrets)

## Server Workflow
1. Which route receives it
2. Validation (e.g. Zod)
3. Mock behaviour when env keys are missing
4. Live AI/DB behaviour when keys exist
5. Normalization / business-rules layers
6. What the UI displays

## Main Files
| Path | Owns |
|------|------|

## What we do not store or build
- …
```

## `features/<slug>.md` required sections
- Purpose  
- User workflow (numbered)  
- Files and responsibilities  
- Data flow and dependencies  
- How to test  
- Out of scope  

## Relationship to Worklog
1. Update `Worklog/` (changelog + short feature note) per `04-worklog.mdc`.  
2. Update `Docs/how-it-works/` for behaviour/flow.  
3. Point the feature Worklog note at the how-it-works path when useful (`Docs/how-it-works/features/<slug>.md`).
